  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>Atom <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">B</mi></math> forms HCP&nbsp;as&nbsp;anions are larger in size.</p><p>From the formula&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">B</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></math>,</p><p>Number of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">B</mi></math> atoms<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn></math>,</p><p>Then, number of tetrahedral voids&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>&#215;</mo></math>Tetrahedral voids<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>6</mn></math>.</p><p>As <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>'</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi><mo>'</mo></math>&nbsp;is occupying tetrahedral voids,</p><p>&nbsp;<math> <mrow> <mfrac> <mn>1</mn> <mn>3</mn> </mfrac> </mrow> </math>&nbsp;of&nbsp;tetrahedral voids<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>3</mn></mfrac><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>6</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></math><br /><br />Therefore, formula of the compound<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">B</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></math></p>"
